    {
      "type": "updated",
      "source": "wgmods",
      "sourceId": "7745",
      "title": "14th_ua's MoE Calculator",
      "previous": {
        "modVersion": "1.6.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.0",
        "fileName": "MoECalculator_1.6.0.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T22:45:28.444Z",
        "changeLog": "Alongside the corner overlay, the mod can now draw a wide progress bar in the centre of the screen during battle. It's off by default — turn it on in the settings panel under Progress Bar, then pick which of the two bars you want.\nMoving Average — where your career projected average combined damage sits between the mark you already hold and the requirement for the next one, with this battle's signed contribution beside it. It comes up whenever that projection moves.\nDamage Efficiency — this battle's combined damage measured against all requirements at once laid out on equal quarters, with every requirement you've already passed lit up."
      },
      "current": {
        "modVersion": "1.7.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.0",
        "fileName": "MoECalculator_1.7.0.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-01T19:16:22.404Z",
        "changeLog": "Improved in-battle percentage prediction.\nThe Progress Bar section now has its own visibility switches.\nBoth centre bars can now be drawn 1.5x as tall and twice as wide.\nThe fade in / hold / fade out can be turned off entirely under Transitions, separately for automatic appearances and for Alt peeks.\nReorganized settings a bit."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "updated",
      "source": "wgmods",
      "sourceId": "7740",
      "title": "Garage Progress Bar",
      "previous": {
        "modVersion": "1.4.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.0",
        "fileName": "GarageProgressBar-Bundle_1.4.0.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-07-30T22:45:43.342Z",
        "changeLog": "Elite Rewards tooltips now tell you which level a reward unlocks at. "
      },
      "current": {
        "modVersion": "1.5.0",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.0",
        "fileName": "GarageProgressBar-Bundle_1.5.0.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-01T19:16:13.989Z",
        "changeLog": "Fully Progressed bar. A vehicle with nothing left to research, upgrade, or unlock used to keep showing a finished Elite Levels bar. It now gets its own golden bar that lists every progression type it completed, with the total XP each one took.\nThe settings panel is grouped. The mod's options in ModsSettingsAPI are now split into Modes, Formatting, and Layout instead of one flat list, so related settings sit together."
      }
    },
